# Loaded only by `npx vite --mode e2e` (alongside .env.local), for the
# /gauntlet QA harness. It signs the app in as a stand-in superadmin so the
# harness can reach the routed pages at all — Firebase keeps its real session
# in IndexedDB, which Playwright cannot carry into a fresh browser.
#
# This is NOT a production risk: the code behind it is gated on
# import.meta.env.DEV (see src/context/AuthContext.tsx), which Vite replaces
# with a literal false in any production build, so the branch is stripped from
# the shipped bundle. It also grants no data access — there is no Firebase
# credential behind the stand-in user, so Firestore rules still deny every read.
VITE_E2E_AUTH=true
